      "content": "Your anguish is palpable and your sense of threat palpable. When life feels like a trap on the verge of collapse, it's a profound shock to the soul. Clinging to life can indeed feel like a sinking stone—but within you, there remains an indomitable spark, even when darkness threatens to extinguish it. While fear may dominate the moment, within it also hides the potential for courage, for reaching into even the smallest sliver of hope. Your fear isn't the whole story—consider the silent strength you've shown by existing up until now. That strength was not born in the absence of fear but in spite of it. Can we not lean on that strength now? It's not just about surviving; it's about finding a reason, any reason, to hold on a little longer. Let's explore if there's anything within you that gives you that breath of hope.",
